---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SkinProfile from '../components/SkinProfile.astro';
import { getRepurchasedPosts } from '../lib/posts';
import { site } from '../site';

const repurchasedPosts = await getRepurchasedPosts();
const repurchasedWithoutReviews = [
  'Mixsoon Cica Hyal Deep Soothing Cream',
];
const repurchasedProducts = [
  ...repurchasedPosts.map((post) => post.data.productName ?? post.data.title),
  ...repurchasedWithoutReviews,
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Kay"
  description="Who writes K-Beauty Truth, how products are chosen, and what this site will not pretend to be."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <section class="stack-page">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 class="page-title">About Kay</h1>
      <p>
        {site.name} is written by Kay. Korean skincare has been part of {site.author.name}'s life for
        as long as she can remember. She has slightly dry, somewhat sensitive skin. The questions she brings
        to a new product are usually about anti-aging and whether her barrier will tolerate it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I document products I have personally purchased and used over time, from the ones I
        finished and repurchased to the ones I stopped using because my skin did not respond well. Unless a note says otherwise, reviewed products are ones Kay bought and used herself.
      </p>
      <p>
        Personal use notes stay separate from researched background. When a page includes context
        that did not come from her own testing, that is written as research or brand information,
        not as her skin result.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before buying, she tends to look into whether a formula seems suitable for sensitive skin.
        She has bought products from Amazon and Olive Young. She is willing to write about products
        that did not suit her.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kay is not a dermatologist, cosmetic chemist, esthetician, or industry expert. Nothing here
        is a diagnosis or a treatment plan.
      </p>
      <SkinProfile />
      <h2>What is on the shelf now</h2>
      <p>These are products Kay has said she is currently using:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>COSRX Advanced Pure Vitamin C 23% Serum with Vitamin E &amp; Glutathione</li>
        <li>Medicube Jelly Mist Serum with Pink PDRN Collagen</li>
        <li>Torriden DIVE IN Cleansing Oil</li>
        <li>Torriden DIVE-IN Low Molecular Hyaluronic Acid Serum</li>
        <li>Torriden DIVE-IN Low Molecular Hyaluronic Acid Soothing Cream</li>
        <li>VT COSMETICS PDRN Daily Hydrating Mask, 30 Sheets</li>
        <li>Medicube PDRN Pink Peptide Serum</li>
        <li>Mixsoon Centella Asiatica Toner</li>
        <li>Medicube Booster Pro X2</li>
        <li>AESTURA ATOBARRIER365 Cream with Ceramides</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Finished and bought again</h2>
      <ul>
        {repurchasedProducts.map((product) => <li>{product}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <h2>Stopped</h2>
      <p>
        Medicube Collagen Jelly Cream with Collagen &amp; Niacinamide. Kay used it, her skin broke
        out, and she is not using it now. That is her result, not a claim that the cream breaks
        everyone out.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/editorial-policy/">How these notes are written</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
